message: "If you use Dailwind Research Tools in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Dailwind Research Tools: Browser-Based Corpus, Text and Document Tools"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tahir
    given-names: Arslan
    affiliation: "Dailwind App Studio; Emerson University, Multan"
  - family-names: Tahir
    given-names: Adnan
    affiliation: "Emerson University, Multan"
version: "2026.11"
date-released: "2026-11-19"
license: MIT
url: "https://dailwind.com/toolkits/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/dailwind/dailwind-website"
abstract: >-
  Dailwind Research Tools is a collection of free, browser-based tools for
  corpus linguistics, text analysis, writing and document work, published by
  Dailwind App Studio. It includes a corpus toolkit (KWIC concordance, word
  lists, collocations, keyness), corpus cleaning, merging and metadata tools,
  register, lexical, readability, stylistic, stylometric, morphological,
  syntactic and sentiment analysis, a parallel text aligner, a qualitative
  coder, a subtitle corpus builder, and writing, OCR, PDF and image utilities.
  Most tools process files locally in the user's browser.
keywords:
  - corpus linguistics
  - text analysis
  - natural language processing
  - concordance
  - research software
  - digital humanities
